-- title:
--   An étale finite R-order spanning A over K is maximal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be an integrally closed integral domain and let $K$ be a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R$. Let $A$ be a commutative ring carrying compatible $K$- and $R$-algebra structures, the $R$-algebra structure being the one induced through $K$ (a scalar-tower hypothesis). Let $S$ be an $R$-subalgebra of $A$ which is finite as an $R$-module and étale as an $R$-algebra, and assume that $S$ spans $A$ over $K$, i.e. the $K$-submodule of $A$ generated by the underlying set of $S$ is all of $A$. The conclusion is the equality of subalgebras $S = \operatorname{integralClosure} R\,A$: every element of $S$ is integral over $R$, and conversely every element of $A$ satisfying a monic polynomial with coefficients in $R$ already lies in $S$. All three types are taken in a single universe.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra core of the uniqueness statement for finite flat models of an étale generic fibre: an order which is finite, étale and of full rank is the maximal order, i.e. the integral closure. It is used in the classification of Hopf orders of prime rank, in the guise of the results on bialgebra maps to monoid algebras that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subalgebra_eq_integralClosure_of_etale_of_span_eq_top.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

theorem Subalgebra.eq_integralClosure_of_etale_of_span_eq_top
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R]
    {K : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [Algebra K A] [Algebra R A] [IsScalarTower R K A]
    (S : Subalgebra R A) [Module.Finite R ↥S] [Algebra.Etale R ↥S]
    (hspan : Submodule.span K (S : Set A) = ⊤) :
    S = integralClosure R A := by sorry
